  'privacy.title': "Privacy",
  /** HTML */
  'privacy.body': "<p>You can use Niflaot <b>without an account</b>: then your progress is kept only in your browser (localStorage) and sent nowhere.</p><h3>Who is responsible</h3><p>The Torah project MyChitas, <a href=\"mailto:Office@mychitas.app\">Office@mychitas.app</a>.</p><h3>What we keep if you create an account</h3><ul><li>your email — to sign in with a code;</li><li>your nickname, age group (14+ or under 14), language;</li><li>for children under 14 — a parent's email and the record of their consent;</li><li>your progress in the lessons and in the Gematria of the Day, points and streak;</li><li>the classes you are in or teach;</li><li>the number of questions to the AI teacher per day (not their text).</li></ul><h3>Why and on what basis</h3><p>To keep your progress on all your devices, to show classes, and to count the questions to the AI teacher. The basis is your consent (Art. 6 (1) a GDPR), for children under 14 — a parent's consent (Art. 8 GDPR, § 4 DSG). You can withdraw consent at any time by deleting the account.</p><h3>Who sees what</h3><p>Your nickname and points — the teacher of a class you join; they are not shown to other players. Nobody but us sees your email.</p><h3>Where it is kept and who helps</h3><ul><li>Cloudflare — the server for accounts, the AI teacher and reminders;</li><li>Resend — sends the sign-in codes and the emails to parents;</li><li>Anthropic — answers the questions to the AI teacher (questions are sent there but not stored by us);</li><li>GitHub Pages — the site itself; GoatCounter — visit statistics without cookies;</li><li>Google, Apple, Mozilla — deliver notifications if you turned them on.</li></ul><h3>How long</h3><p>As long as the account exists. A child's account without a parent's consent is deleted after 30 days, an unfinished sign-up after 7 days.</p><h3>Your rights</h3><p>You can ask what data we keep about you, correct it or delete it — the “Delete account” button on the account page deletes everything at once. Questions — to <a href=\"mailto:Office@mychitas.app\">Office@mychitas.app</a>. You can also complain to the Austrian Data Protection Authority (Datenschutzbehörde, dsb.gv.at).</p>",
